1. Prefix substrings (start at index `0`)

```python
s = "aabcb"

for i in range(len(s)):
    print(s[:i+1])
```

Time: `O(n)`

2. Suffix substrings (end at last index)

```python
s = "aabcb"

for i in range(len(s)):
    print(s[i:])
```

Time: `O(n)`

3. All continuous substrings (general substrings)

```python
s = "aabcb"

for i in range(len(s)):
    for j in range(i, len(s)):
        print(s[i:j+1])
```

Time: `O(n²)` substrings generated

4. All subsequences (non-continuous allowed)

```python
from itertools import combinations

s = "aabcb"

for r in range(1, len(s)+1):
    for comb in combinations(range(len(s)), r):
        print("".join(s[i] for i in comb))
```

Time: `O(2ⁿ)` because subsequences grow exponentially.



